/* Finnish — the development language, and deliberately empty.

   Every user-facing string in this app is written in Finnish directly in the
   SwiftUI source, and SwiftUI treats a string literal in Text, Button, Label,
   navigationTitle and accessibilityLabel as a LocalizedStringKey. A key with no
   entry in the table renders as itself, so the Finnish text IS the key and IS
   the fallback. Filling this file with "Kerro" = "Kerro"; pairs would add a
   second copy of every string that has to be kept in step with the first, and
   the day it drifts the app shows the stale half.

   The file exists at all for one reason: without a fi.lproj the bundle declares
   only English, and iOS will hand a Finnish device the English table — which is
   the app speaking the wrong language to the one person it was built for.

   The translations live in en.lproj/Localizable.strings. To read the Finnish,
   read the source. */
